# Firebase (kryteria A + B + 14)

## Pakiety (SDK 54)

```bash
npx expo install firebase expo-secure-store expo-auth-session expo-web-browser
```

Używaj **Firebase JS SDK** (`firebase/app`, `firebase/auth`, `firebase/firestore`) — kompatybilny z Expo Go.

## Zmienne środowiskowe

Plik `.env` (w `.gitignore`):

```
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
```

```typescript
// src/services/firebase/config.ts
const firebaseConfig = {
  apiKey: process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY,
  authDomain: process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN,
  projectId: process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID,
  // ...
};
```

**NIGDY** nie hardcoduj kluczy w plikach `.ts`/`.tsx`.

## SecureStore — token sesji (kryterium 14)

```typescript
// src/lib/storage/secure-storage.ts
import * as SecureStore from 'expo-secure-store';

const TOKEN_KEY = 'firebase_id_token';

export async function saveAuthToken(token: string) {
  await SecureStore.setItemAsync(TOKEN_KEY, token);
}
export async function getAuthToken() {
  return SecureStore.getItemAsync(TOKEN_KEY);
}
export async function clearAuthToken() {
  await SecureStore.deleteItemAsync(TOKEN_KEY);
}
```

Wrażliwe dane **NIE** w AsyncStorage.

## Auth — Email + Google (kryterium B: min. 2 metody)

```typescript
// src/services/firebase/auth.ts
import { createUserWithEmailAndPassword, signInWithEmailAndPassword, signOut } from 'firebase/auth';
import * as Google from 'expo-auth-session/providers/google';
import { GoogleAuthProvider, signInWithCredential } from 'firebase/auth';

// Email
export const registerWithEmail = (email: string, password: string) =>
  createUserWithEmailAndPassword(auth, email, password);

export const loginWithEmail = (email: string, password: string) =>
  signInWithEmailAndPassword(auth, email, password);

// Google — expo-auth-session + credential
// Web Client ID z Firebase Console → Authentication → Google
```

## Auto-login po restarcie

```typescript
// AuthContext — onAuthStateChanged
useEffect(() => {
  const unsub = onAuthStateChanged(auth, async (user) => {
    if (user) {
      const token = await user.getIdToken();
      await saveAuthToken(token);
    } else {
      await clearAuthToken();
    }
    dispatch({ type: 'SET_USER', payload: user });
  });
  return unsub;
}, []);
```

## Firestore schema

```
users/{uid}/cycles/{cycleId}
  startDate: string   // ISO "2026-01-15"
  endDate?: string    // ISO, opcjonalnie
  notes?: string
  createdAt: Timestamp
  updatedAt: Timestamp
```

```typescript
// src/types/cycle.ts
export type Cycle = {
  id: string;
  startDate: string;
  endDate?: string;
  notes?: string;
  createdAt: string;
};
```

## CRUD — `src/services/firebase/cycles.ts`

Każda funkcja zwraca `Promise<Cycle>` lub rzuca `FirebaseError`. Context obsługuje loading/error.

```typescript
import { collection, doc, addDoc, getDocs, updateDoc, deleteDoc, query, orderBy } from 'firebase/firestore';

export async function fetchCycles(uid: string): Promise<Cycle[]> {
  const q = query(collection(db, 'users', uid, 'cycles'), orderBy('startDate', 'desc'));
  const snap = await getDocs(q);
  return snap.docs.map(d => ({ id: d.id, ...d.data() } as Cycle));
}
```

## Firestore Security Rules (w Firebase Console)

```javascript
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /users/{userId}/cycles/{cycleId} {
      allow read, write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;
    }
  }
}
```

## Chronione ekrany

Niezalogowany użytkownik **nie** widzi `(tabs)/*` — tylko `(auth)/login` i `(auth)/register`.

## Async pattern w Context

```typescript
const addCycle = async (data: Omit<Cycle, 'id'>) => {
  dispatch({ type: 'FETCH_START' });
  try {
    const cycle = await createCycle(user.uid, data);
    dispatch({ type: 'ADD_CYCLE', payload: cycle });
    await Haptics.notificationAsync(Haptics.NotificationFeedbackType.Success);
  } catch (e) {
    dispatch({ type: 'FETCH_ERROR', payload: mapFirebaseError(e) });
  }
};
```
